  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent history shows persistent downward drift and sentiment is negative.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias when true outcomes deviate significantly from recent 5-day average, especially in low-sentiment periods.",
    "Lower forecast peaks when sentiment history includes multiple negative entries (e.g., >2 consecutive negative sentiment values).",
    "Increase downward bias in forecasts when true outcomes consistently underperform model predictions in the 10-day window following a high forecast.",
    "Treat sentiment history as a volatility filter: if sentiment is negative, reduce forecast magnitude by 5–10% to account for downward pressure."
  ]
}
